  "conventions": {
    "fact_encoding": "facts.<name> = {type, value, state}; state in {user_confirmed, extracted_candidate, derived, missing, conflicting}. money = {amount_minor:int, currency}. datetime = ISO-8601 with offset.",
    "paths": "R04.a = bag-fee refund (14 CFR 260.5); R04.b = delayed-bag incidental expenses (14 CFR 254.4 + DOT guidance); R04.c = lost/damaged property (14 CFR 254.4). Each case names the path(s) it tests.",
    "delay_measurement": "From deplane opportunity to delivery/pickup (260.5(a)). 'Within 12 hours' is inclusive of exactly 12:00 (spec assumption A1).",
    "liability_floor": "USD 4,700 per passenger for incidents on/after 2025-01-22; USD 3,800 before (FR-2024-23588). It is the lowest cap a carrier may impose, never an expected payout.",
    "carrier_contract_terms": "No carrier contract of carriage is captured in v1, so paths b/c are capped at likely_eligible_missing_evidence and their claim deadlines are unknown.",
    "outcome_vocabulary": [
      "eligible",
      "likely_eligible_missing_evidence",
      "possible_contract_benefit",
      "needs_facts",
      "manual_review",
      "not_eligible",
      "deadline_passed",
      "source_unverified",
      "unsupported",
      "not_yet_due"
    ],
    "loader": "A case has EITHER a top-level `expected` OR an `expected` on every variant. `clock` (and optional `source`) may be set on the case or on a variant; a variant value overrides the case value. `facts_from: <case id>` + `facts_override: {...}` means: copy that case's facts, then replace the named facts. A variant's `change` object replaces the named facts for that variant only. Every `facts` value is an object; no prose placeholders.",
    "fact_states": "user_confirmed | observed | derived | extracted_candidate | conflicting | missing | assumption. Contract §2.5 mapping: user_confirmed→confirmed, observed→observed, derived→derived, extracted_candidate→candidate, conflicting→conflicting, missing→missing (value null), assumption→assumption-class candidate. D147(2)/X1: `eligible` requires every decisive fact to be user_confirmed, or observed/derived from confirmed facts; an extracted_candidate decisive fact caps the outcome at likely_eligible_missing_evidence (the case lists it in expected.unconfirmed_decisive_facts). Since M2D the baseline cases use user_confirmed for decisive facts (the state after the user's fact review); each file has explicit cap variants.",
    "conflicting": "A conflicting fact carries `candidates: [{value, evidence, ...}]` (README cross-pack rule 3). If every candidate gives the same outcome the conflict is not material, but the fact is still unconfirmed, so the outcome is capped at likely_eligible_missing_evidence; if candidates diverge the outcome is needs_facts. Advisory dates use the earliest candidate.",
    "not_yet_due": "D147(6)/X3: a path that is not ripe yet has outcome not_yet_due with expected.reevaluate_at (ISO date) or expected.reevaluate_when (event); never not_eligible.",
    "missing_source": "X5: a variant with source.record = 'missing' means no current source record exists for the pack → source_unverified.",
    "path_a_eligible": "D147(1): path a (bag-fee refund, 260.5) may reach eligible when its decisive facts are confirmed; the likely_eligible cap applies to paths b and c only (no carrier contract of carriage captured)."
  },
